---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
const title = "Methodology";
---

<Layout title={title}>
  <h1 style="font-size: 34px; margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #111827;">Methodology</h1>

  <p style="margin: 0 0 18px 0; color: #374151; max-width: 860px; line-height: 1.65;">
    Redline Report studies markets through the interaction of cycles, fundamentals and expectations. We start with primary data and financial evidence, develop an independent thesis, and focus on situations where market expectations may diverge from underlying fundamentals.
  </p>

  <div class="rule-grid">
    <section class="rule-card">
      <h2>Evidence hierarchy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tier 1:</strong> regulatory filings, audited financial statements, official statistics and primary market data.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2:</strong> earnings calls, company disclosures, industry data and official policy documents.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 3:</strong> credible third-party research, investigative reporting and alternative datasets.</li>
        <li><strong>Not evidence:</strong> unsupported narratives, promotional claims or data without a traceable source.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rule-card">
      <h2>HOW WE RESEARCH</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We separate <strong>facts</strong> from <strong>interpretation</strong> explicitly.</li>
        <li>We distinguish <strong>structural trends from cyclical movements</strong>.</li>
        <li>We compare <strong>market expectations with underlying fundamentals</strong>.</li>
        <li>We define what evidence would <strong>invalidate the thesis</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rule-card">
      <h2>What we examine</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cycles:</strong> macroeconomic, credit, commodity and industry cycles.</li>
        <li><strong>Companies:</strong> business models, financial quality, capital allocation and governance.</li>
        <li><strong>Industries:</strong> supply, demand, capacity, cost curves and competitive structure.</li>
        <li><strong>Markets:</strong> valuation, positioning, expectations and potential mispricing.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rule-card">
      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No insider information or MNPI.</li>
        <li>No personalized investment advice.</li>
        <li>No price targets presented as certainty.</li>
          <li>No claims of predictive certainty or guaranteed market outcomes.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="rule-footer">
    <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
    <p>
      If a material error is identified, we publish a correction with a visible change note.
      If you dispute a claim, bring primary evidence—not opinions.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .rule-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 14px;
    max-width: 960px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .rule-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  .rule-card {
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px 16px;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .rule-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #111827;
  }
  .rule-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .rule-card li { margin: 6px 0; }
  .rule-footer {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    max-width: 860px;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .rule-footer h2 {
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #111827;
  }
</style>